## Linear conventions

- `assignee: "me"` for current user.
- Priority map: `P0=Urgent(1)`, `P1=High(2)`, `P2=Medium(3)`, `P3=Low(4)`.
- Never auto-complete or auto-transition status.
{{ end }}

## Repo resolution

Read the repo registry named in the installed profile context.

Checkout layout under `~/src/`:

- `~/src/<org>/<repo>`: org parents are `base/` (github.com/base), `protocols/` and
  `coinbase/` (Coinbase GHE), `0x00101010/` (own GitHub: `dotfiles`, the context
  repository named above, own tools), and upstream orgs (`ethereum-optimism/`,
  `paradigmxyz/`, `commonware/`, ...). Parents are not repos; always use the sub-path.
  Top-level `~/src/<repo>` dirs are older clones that predate this convention.
- Bare layout (`.bare/` plus a `.git` file): worktrees are sibling dirs. Work in
  `<repo>/main` or `<repo>/master`, never in the parent. `dev<N>` siblings mark a slot
  repo: `devslot claim <branch>` / `devslot release`.
- Standard layout: ordinary `.git/`; work in the checkout itself.

Don't guess silently — ambiguous topic → list candidates and ask.

## Universal rules

- Never fabricate entries, findings, or sources.
- Never auto-complete the user's todos or Linear issues.
- Always present drafts and get confirmation before destructive writes.
- Surgical writes only — touch only the files the skill is meant to touch.
- Preserve the user's voice; don't embellish prose.
